message: "If you cite this computational research thesis, please use the metadata below. No DOI is minted here; do not invent one."
type: thesis
title: "Host infection windows that re-rank channel–profile composition without merging into Θ"
authors:
  - family-names: Ogbonna
    given-names: Kelechi Emeka
    email: kelechiogbonna300@gmail.com
    alias: cloudynirvana
abstract: >-
  Can declared host infection windows that re-rank immunometabolic
  hypotheses also change which named observation-channel compositions
  remain legal Disease Profiles, without promoting either the windows
  or the channel coefficients into Θ? They can. Sixteen composition
  files were scored by the disjoint-union rule list and by a schedule
  clause. Seven files pass the structural list. The ledger schedule
  accepts five. The host schedule, which adds the declared windows
  [1.5, 2.5] and [10, 12], accepts one (windowed). Four files leave
  and none enters. The JSON Schema accept set is eleven files on both
  schedules. SHA-256 of the canonical kinetic object does not change,
  including after a refused promotion of k_inf and k_host. Research
  only. Not a medical device. No document DOI.
keywords:
